        "original_id": "13b2f77d-f514-5815-94c5-714f06933af1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jack Young, Arthur Payne\n- Events: 1952 Individual Speedway World Championship, London Riders' Championship\n- Topics: speedway, championship results\n\nFacts:\n- In 1952, Jack Young won his second straight Speedway World Championship with 14 points.\n- In 1952, Jack Young became the first rider to win the Speedway World Championship twice and the first rider to win it in consecutive years.\n- In 1952, Arthur Payne finished fifth in the Speedway World Championship final.\n- Arthur Payne was born on 28 August 1923 in Sydney, New South Wales.\n- Jack Young won the London Riders' Championship in 1953 and 1954.\n- Jack Young was a nine-time South Australian Champion between 1948 and 1964.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
